  "description": "<p>Build an SEO client questionnaire that asks each client type its own questions and saves the answers to a database you own.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"SEO Client Questionnaire FAQ\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an SEO client questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"An SEO client questionnaire is the set of questions an agency or consultant sends a new client before work starts. It collects the business type, goals, competitors, target searches, past SEO history, and which tools the client can grant access to. The strategist then starts the kickoff call with facts in hand.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an SEO client questionnaire?\", \"a\": \"Describe it to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a> in one prompt. Name the kinds of clients you take on, the questions each kind answers, the tools you need access to, and who gets alerted about which answers. Emergent builds the questionnaire, a database of client records, and a dashboard, and you change any part of it by prompting again.\"}, {\"q\": \"What questions should an SEO client questionnaire include?\", \"a\": \"Cover five areas: the business and what it sells, goals and how success is measured, customers and competitors, the site's history, and access. History means past agencies and any penalty. Access means which tools the client has added you to. Then add questions that apply only to that client's type, such as office locations for a local business.\"}, {\"q\": \"How far before the kickoff call should an SEO client questionnaire go out?\", \"a\": \"Send it at least a few days before the kickoff call, as soon as the contract is signed. The answers can then shape the agenda. If you already send a general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/client-onboarding-questionnaire'>client onboarding questionnaire</a>, add the SEO questions to it instead of sending a second form that asks for the company details again.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many questions should an SEO client questionnaire have?\", \"a\": \"Aim for about 20 and stop at 30. Offer choices wherever a list will do, such as business type or the month sales peak, and save open text for goals and history. Emergent can build the questions to branch by client type. A store owner then never scrolls past questions written for a dental office.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an SEO questionnaire ask clients for their passwords?\", \"a\": \"No. Ask the client to add you as a user in each tool, and list those tools in the questionnaire with a checkbox each. In Google Analytics, the person adding you needs the Administrator role at the account or property level. Ask the client who on their side holds it.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one SEO client questionnaire work for local businesses and online stores?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as long as the first question asks for the business type and the questions after it depend on the answer. Each client skips the other type's questions, which keeps the form short. The same branching suits an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/interior-design-questionnaire'>interior design questionnaire</a>, where the room being redone decides what comes next.\"}, {\"q\": \"How can an SEO client questionnaire uncover a past penalty?\", \"a\": \"Ask in the questionnaire, then open the Manual actions report in Search Console once you have access. Google issues a manual action when a human reviewer finds pages that break its spam policies, and it notifies site owners in that report and in the Search Console message center. Ask for the year and the cause as well.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I do with SEO client questionnaire answers before kickoff?\", \"a\": \"Turn them into the agenda. Put risks first, such as a past penalty or missing access, then goals, then competitors and target searches. In an app Emergent builds, each submission is saved to a database you own, and the app can lay out the agenda from that record. Nobody copies answers by hand.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does an SEO client questionnaire ask that a design brief does not?\", \"a\": \"It asks about search: the terms buyers type, the competitors that show up in results, the site's history, and tool access. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/logo-design-questionnaire'>logo design questionnaire</a> asks about style and where the logo will appear. If a client needs both, send them as separate forms so each set of answers reaches the right person.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
